    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d384-a3">

                <pb facs="0868" n="784" sameAs="frus:frus1886/pg784"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2 in No. 340.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Hidalgo &amp; Co. to Mr.
                            Williams.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Havana</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1885-12-11"><hi rendition="#italic">December</hi> 11,
                        1885</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Sir</hi>: In answer to your letter of the 9th
                    instant we beg first to refer you as regards the payment of tonnage dues on
                    steamers of the Alexandre and Ward lines, to paragraphs 112 and 113 of the
                    latest edition of the customs tariff, where you will find a <pb facs="0869"
                        n="785" xml:id="pg785"/> copy of a royal decree dated Madrid, 25th August,
                    1867, which deals with the matter. Secondly we have to answer your questions as
                    follows: <list>
                        <item>To the first. We pay duties according to net registered tonnage, less
                            6 tons.</item>
                        <item>To the second. Sixty-two and one-half cents per 1,000 kilograms of
                            cargo imported and exported.</item>
                    </list></p>
                <p>We have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>HIDALGO &amp; CO.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
